Upstream timer: dudect.h includes <emmintrin.h> and <x86intrin.h> and defines cpucycles() as _mm_mfence() then
__rdtsc(). It has no AArch64 branch at this commit, so it does not compile on arm64.

armShim/ holds two headers found before the system ones (-isystem) on AArch64 only. They supply the two names
cpucycles() calls: _mm_mfence() as `dsb sy` and __rdtsc() as `isb; mrs cntvct_el0`. The pinned header stays untouched
and its statistics (Welch t-test, percentile crops, second-order test, thresholds 10 and 500) run as upstream wrote them.
The AArch64 counter is the generic timer (cntfrq_el0 Hz; read 1000000000 on an Apple M3 Max under macOS, and 1e8 ticks
measured 100.0 ms against CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW), not a CPU cycle counter.
x25519Dudect.sh refuses a dudect.h whose sha256 differs from the one above.
